    4. Place sprites in the OUTPUT settled against their wall (cols 1-3 for left,
       W-4 to W-2 for right), processing nearest-first so each new sprite abuts
       the wall or a previously placed same-color sprite. Verify no cross-color
       pixel overlap; reject/retry on collision.
    5. Derive INPUT by shifting each sprite horizontally away from its wall by a
       random offset (1-5 cols), clamping to stay within cols 1..W-2. Verify no
       overlap with other sprites or opposite wall column; retry offset if needed.
    6. Validate by running solver on input and comparing to output.

